tp://pyfpdf.googlecode.com/)\n/Title (Answer Sheet - Physics, Maths, Chemistry, Biology, General_Knowledge)\n/CreationDate (D:20260326143826)\n>>\nendobj\n12 0 obj\n<<\n/Type /Catalog\n/Pages 1 0 R\n/OpenAction [3 0 R /FitH null]\n/PageLayout /OneColumn\n>>\nendobj\nxref\n0 13\n0000000000 65535 f \n0000003480 00000 n \n0000003777 00000 n \n0000000009 00000 n \n0000000087 00000 n \n0000001437 00000 n \n0000001515 00000 n \n0000002575 00000 n \n0000002653 00000 n \n0000003579 00000 n \n0000003680 00000 n \n0000003892 00000 n \n0000004080 00000 n \ntrailer\n<<\n/Size 13\n/Root 12 0 R\n/Info 11 0 R\n>>\nstartxref\n4184\n%%EOF\n','2026-03-26 14:38:26','everyone','2026-03-26 09:08:26','[{\"question\": \"What is the primary method of reproduction in humans?\", \"options\": [\"Asexual reproduction\", \"Binary fission\", \"Ovulation\", \"Sexual reproduction\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Humans reproduce sexually, involving the fusion of sperm and an egg cell.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In plants, which of the following is a common method of asexual reproduction?\", \"options\": [\"Mitosis\", \"Fission\", \"Budding\", \"Vegetative propagation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation involves the growth of a new plant from parts of an existing plant, such as stems, leaves, or roots.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is an example of asexual reproduction in fungi?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fusion of hyphae\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Oviparity\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation in fungi involves growing new individuals from parts of the existing organism, such as mycelium.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following best describes binary fission in prokaryotes?\", \"options\": [\"Cell division of a single prokaryotic cell into two daughter cells\", \"Asexual reproduction by fragmentation\", \"Sexual reproduction involving the fusion of gametes\", \"Vegetative propagation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Binary fission is the process by which a single prokaryotic cell divides into two identical daughter cells.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a method of asexual reproduction in amoebas?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Conjugation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Fusion of gametes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Binary fission in amoebas involves the division of the cell into two daughter cells.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In which of the following organisms does asexual reproduction typically occur through vegetative propagation?\", \"options\": [\"Plants\", \"Protozoa\", \"Fungi\", \"All of the above\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation is a common method of asexual reproduction in plants, fungi, and certain protozoa.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"How does the process of meiosis differ from mitosis in terms of chromosome number?\", \"options\": [\"Meiosis has twice as many chromosomes as mitosis\", \"Mitosis results in four cells, meiosis results in two\", \"Meiosis results in a diploid cell, mitosis results in a haploid cell\", \"Both have the same number of chromosomes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Meiosis reduces the chromosome number from diploid (2n) to haploid (n), while mitosis maintains the diploid chromosome number.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In which of the following organisms does asexual reproduction typically occur through fragmentation?\", \"options\": [\"Protozoa\", \"Plants\", \"Bacteria\", \"All of the above\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Fragmentation is a method of asexual reproduction in protozoa, plants, and certain bacteria.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following statements is true regarding binary fission in prokaryotes?\", \"options\": [\"It is a complex process involving multiple steps\", \"It results in two identical daughter cells\", \"It involves the fusion of gametes\", \"It is the same as mitosis\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"Binary fission in prokaryotes involves the division of a single cell into two identical daughter cells.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of sexual reproduction?\", \"options\": [\"Asexual reproduction by budding\", \"Fission\", \"Oviparity\", \"Fusion of gametes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Sexual reproduction in organisms involves the fusion of gametes from two parents.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In which of the following organisms does vegetative propagation typically occur?\", \"options\": [\"Protozoa\", \"Plants\", \"Fungi\", \"All of the above\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation involves the growth of a new plant from parts of an existing plant, such as stems, leaves, or roots.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"How does asexual reproduction differ from sexual reproduction in terms of gamete formation?\", \"options\": [\"Asexual reproduction requires the fusion of gametes\", \"Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of gametes\", \"Asexual reproduction does not involve the fusion of gametes\", \"Both require the fusion of gametes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Asexual reproduction does not involve the fusion of gametes; instead, it involves the division of existing cells or organisms into new individuals.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of vegetative propagation in plants?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Fission\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation in plants involves the growth of new plants from parts of the existing plant, such as stems, leaves, or roots.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of asexual reproduction in protozoa?\", \"options\": [\"Mitosis\", \"Binary fission\", \"Conjugation\", \"Fragmentation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"Binary fission is a method of asexual reproduction in protozoa involving the division of a single cell into two daughter cells.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of sexual reproduction in plants?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Fusion of gametes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Sexual reproduction in plants involves the fusion of gametes from two parents.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In which of the following organisms does vegetative propagation typically occur?\", \"options\": [\"Protozoa\", \"Plants\", \"Bacteria\", \"All of the above\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation is a common method of asexual reproduction in protozoa, plants, and certain bacteria.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of asexual reproduction in fungi?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Conjugation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation in fungi involves growing new individuals from parts of the existing organism, such as mycelium.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of asexual reproduction in plants?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Conjugation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Vegetative propagation in plants involves the growth of new plants from parts of the existing plant, such as stems, leaves, or roots.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of sexual reproduction in protozoa?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Fusion of gametes\"], \"correct_answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"Sexual reproduction in protozoa involves the fusion of gametes from two individuals.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct example of asexual reproduction in bacteria?\", \"options\": [\"Binary fission\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Vegetative propagation\", \"Conjugation\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"Fragmentation is a method of asexual reproduction in bacteria involving the division of the cell into smaller pieces.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}]'),(4,'2026-03-30','10','1.maths - statistics, areas related to circles, circles, arithmetic progressions\n2.science - sustainable management of natural resources, our environment, sources of energy, electricity, human eye and the colourful world, light ,  reflection and refraction, heredity and evolution, how do organisms reproduce?, control and coordination, life processes, periodic classification of elements, carbon and its compounds, metals and non-metals, acids, bases and salts, chemical reactions and equations',NULL,_binary '%PDF-1.3\n3 0 obj\n<</Type /Page\n/Parent 1 0 R\n/Resources 2 0 R\n/Contents 4 0 R>>\nendobj\n4 0 obj\n<</Filter /FlateDecode /Length 1177>>\nstream\nxœ¥VM\Û6½\çWÌ±lFÔ—¥½»›¦M¿ z)P\Ğ%1¡I—¤\ìø\ßwHI^yµm\\ôdY¢\ŞÌ¼÷fF1üô*\"\ÙN¯¶ğ\æ=š’(‚m\ßoı­MB²6eF\è¶5|÷(™µ@#XÃ¯\Ìuv»³^<v|/¬3\ç<-u‹?p\Å\r“ş¬ôIòº\å¯aûy\Ä~ó>\Z_…·\èÕ­„Z\Â&OIQ†\Ş1\Ç\ï \â|%\ë8Ÿ!gÓ˜\Äô)\Û;Lwyˆ–$KÂ¡Oı\î3¯\Ü\İÿ.h@\ÎËœY@ş…[«\Æ\'{œY\ÇBxf8³`¸Ä‚jp\Z*a*\Éñ\É\å‚\áº=\Çóp0º5ˆ\'´²SLJrš\Âö4¾I	-Bğ˜\ØJpUq¶\ÇÀB±\ä°gŠµ|Ï•İ€b®\Çz0\r«{Sù ø\\…\ÑÊŸZÁø\Ä÷\Õ{\Z¸DÆŒ¨„;¯¦l\"B“\è:›Œ’,\n\Ùt=\Æ~\æÀ\Ûq¨\Ñ\Ş4½„“6²^m\ç`˜K\ã\á±\Òpÿ\Zş® \ã†\×4<\àG-ûñ¾>A­A›–)a÷†bR&›\ëœ\â‚q\È\Ép$µ\î+ş)\×\Ê-n¥µ©‘­ZŠ†{ö‘\ë\é9p#tŠT\Ş\\¢U8Ø‘W¯ 3»1}\á.\Ù<c\'\Ê	ŒR\éıA÷ª\Æ7Qm&mxSiµş¢*\áŸ\î\æZ&C \ï\Ñ*8p4<\åõ!+{\Õoôy¿\r‰dJŠ¡(•>\n(Ş£	 \rw^:‚ÀA;,T0ùöy