j\n11 0 obj\n<<\n/Producer (PyFPDF 1.7.2 http://pyfpdf.googlecode.com/)\n/Title (Answer Sheet - Maths, Physics, Chemistry, General_Knowledge, Biology)\n/CreationDate (D:20260326172327)\n>>\nendobj\n12 0 obj\n<<\n/Type /Catalog\n/Pages 1 0 R\n/OpenAction [3 0 R /FitH null]\n/PageLayout /OneColumn\n>>\nendobj\nxref\n0 13\n0000000000 65535 f \n0000003907 00000 n \n0000004204 00000 n \n0000000009 00000 n \n0000000087 00000 n \n0000001410 00000 n \n0000001488 00000 n \n0000002688 00000 n \n0000002766 00000 n \n0000004006 00000 n \n0000004107 00000 n \n0000004319 00000 n \n0000004507 00000 n \ntrailer\n<<\n/Size 13\n/Root 12 0 R\n/Info 11 0 R\n>>\nstartxref\n4611\n%%EOF\n','2026-03-26 17:23:27','everyone','2026-03-26 11:53:27','[{\"question\": \"The radius of a circle is 5 units. What is the area of the circle?\", \"options\": [\"25\\u03c0\", \"25\", \"5\\u03c0\", \"10\\u03c0\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Area of a circle is given by \\\\( A = \\\\pi r^2 \\\\). With \\\\( r = 5 \\\\) units, the area is \\\\( 25\\\\pi \\\\) square units.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"Which of the following represents the sum of the first 5 natural numbers?\", \"options\": [\"20\", \"15\", \"10\", \"5\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"The sum of the first \\\\( n \\\\) natural numbers is given by \\\\( S = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\\\). For \\\\( n = 5 \\\\), the sum is \\\\( 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If a point (x, y) lies on the circle \\\\( x^2 + y^2 = 16 \\\\), what is the maximum value of \\\\( x + y \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"4\", \"8\", \"2\", \"0\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"To find the maximum value of \\\\( x + y \\\\) on the circle, we can use the constraint \\\\( x^2 + y^2 = 16 \\\\). By symmetry, the maximum value occurs at \\\\( (x, y) = (4, 0) \\\\) or \\\\( (0, 4) \\\\). Thus, \\\\( x + y = 4 \\\\) is the maximum.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"What is the probability of getting a head when a coin is tossed?\", \"options\": [\"0.25\", \"0.5\", \"0.75\", \"1\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"The probability of getting a head in a fair coin toss is \\\\( \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"What is the value of \\\\( \\\\sin(30^\\\\circ) \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"0.5\", \"1\", \"0.707\", \"0.866\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The sine of \\\\( 30^\\\\circ \\\\) is \\\\( \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If the roots of the equation \\\\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\\\) are 2 and -3, what is the value of \\\\( a \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Given the roots, the quadratic equation can be written as \\\\( a(x - 2)(x + 3) = 0 \\\\). Expanding this, we get \\\\( a(x^2 + x - 6) = 0 \\\\). Thus, the coefficient of \\\\( x^2 \\\\) is \\\\( a \\\\), and \\\\( a = 1 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the equation \\\\( 2x^2 - 5x + 3 = 0 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"[1, 1.5]\", \"[1.5, 1]\", \"[0.5, 2]\", \"[2, 0.5]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The roots can be found using the quadratic formula \\\\( x = \\frac{-b \\\\pm \\\\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\\\). For \\\\( 2x^2 - 5x + 3 = 0 \\\\), \\\\( a = 2 \\\\), \\\\( b = -5 \\\\), and \\\\( c = 3 \\\\). Plugging in, the roots are \\\\( 1 \\\\) and \\\\( 1.5 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"What is the value of \\\\( \\\\cos(45^\\\\circ) \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"0.707\", \"0.5\", \"1\", \"0.25\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The cosine of \\\\( 45^\\\\circ \\\\) is \\\\( \\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\approx 0.707 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"A point P(3, 4) lies in the first quadrant. What is the distance of point P from the origin?\", \"options\": [\"5\", \"2.5\", \"4\", \"3\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The distance \\\\( d \\\\) from the origin to point \\\\( (x, y) \\\\) is given by \\\\( d = \\\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} \\\\). For \\\\( P(3, 4) \\\\), \\\\( d = \\\\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = \\\\sqrt{9 + 16} = \\\\sqrt{25} = 5 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the inequality \\\\( 2x + 3 < 9 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"[1, \\u221e)\", \"(-\\u221e, 3]\", \"[0, 3]\", \"[1, 3]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Solving \\\\( 2x + 3 < 9 \\\\), we get \\\\( 2x < 6 \\\\) or \\\\( x < 3 \\\\). Thus, the solution set is \\\\( [0, 3) \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \\\\) are\", \"options\": [\"[1, 6]\", \"[2, 3]\", \"[3, 2]\", \"[6, 1]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"The roots of the quadratic equation \\\\( x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \\\\) can be found by factoring: \\\\( (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0 \\\\). Thus, the roots are \\\\( x = 2 \\\\) and \\\\( x = 3 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 = 0 \\\\) are\", \"options\": [\"[2, 2]\", \"[4, 4]\", \"[2, -2]\", \"[4, -4]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 = 0 \\\\) can be found by recognizing it as a perfect square: \\\\( (x - 2)^2 = 0 \\\\). Thus, the root is \\\\( x = 2 \\\\) (repeated).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If \\\\( a + b = 5 \\\\) and \\\\( ab = 6 \\\\), what is the value of \\\\( a^2 + b^2 \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"25\", \"19\", \"17\", \"13\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"Using the identity \\\\( a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab \\\\), we substitute \\\\( a + b = 5 \\\\) and \\\\( ab = 6 \\\\). Thus, \\\\( a^2 + b^2 = 5^2 - 2 \\\\cdot 6 = 25 - 12 = 13 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 2x - 8 = 0 \\\\) are\", \"options\": [\"[4, -2]\", \"[2, -4]\", \"[2, 4]\", \"[-2, -4]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 2x - 8 = 0 \\\\) can be found by factoring: \\\\( (x - 4)(x + 2) = 0 \\\\). Thus, the roots are \\\\( x = 4 \\\\) and \\\\( x = -2 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The sum of the first 10 terms of the arithmetic progression \\\\( 1, 3, 5, 7, \\\\ldots \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"100\", \"50\", \"75\", \"105\"], \"correct_answer\": \"C\", \"explanation\": \"The sum of the first \\\\( n \\\\) terms of an arithmetic progression is given by \\\\( S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d) \\\\), where \\\\( a \\\\) is the first term and \\\\( d \\\\) is the common difference. For \\\\( a = 1 \\\\), \\\\( d = 2 \\\\), and \\\\( n = 10 \\\\), the sum is \\\\( S_{10} = \\frac{10}{2} (2 \\\\cdot 1 + 9 \\\\cdot 2) = 5 (2 + 18) = 5 \\\\cdot 20 = 100 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If \\\\( \\\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2} \\\\) and \\\\( \\theta \\\\) is in the first quadrant, what is the value of \\\\( \\\\cos(\\theta) \\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"0.707\", \"0.5\", \"1\", \"0.25\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Given \\\\( \\\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2} \\\\) and \\\\( \\theta \\\\) is in the first quadrant, the cosine value is \\\\( \\\\cos(\\theta) = \\\\sqrt{1 - \\\\sin^2(\\theta)} = \\\\sqrt{1 - \\\\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^2} = \\\\sqrt{1 - \\frac{1}{4}} = \\\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} = \\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\approx 0.707 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the inequality \\\\( -x^2 + 4x - 3 > 0 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"(-\\u221e, 1)\", \"(-\\u221e, 3)\", \"(1, 3)\", \"(3, \\u221e)\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The inequality \\\\( -x^2 + 4x - 3 > 0 \\\\) can be rewritten as \\\\( -(x^2 - 4x + 3) > 0 \\\\) or \\\\( (x - 1)(x - 3) < 0 \\\\). The roots are \\\\( x = 1 \\\\) and \\\\( x = 3 \\\\). The solution set is \\\\( (-\\u221e, 1) \\\\cup (3, \\u221e) \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"[1, 6]\", \"[2, 3]\", \"[3, 2]\", \"[6, 1]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \\\\) can be found by factoring: \\\\( (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0 \\\\). Thus, the roots are \\\\( x = 2 \\\\) and \\\\( x = 3 \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the inequality \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 > 0 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"[2, \\u221e)\", \"(-\\u221e, 2)\", \"[1, \\u221e)\", \"(-\\u221e, -2)\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The inequality \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 > 0 \\\\) can be rewritten as \\\\( (x - 2)^2 > 0 \\\\). This is true for all \\\\( x \\neq 2 \\\\). Thus, the solution set is \\\\( (-\\u221e, 2) \\\\cup (2, \\u221e) \\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"The solution set of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 = 0 \\\\) is\", \"options\": [\"[2, 2]\", \"[4, 4]\", \"[2, -2]\", \"[4, -4]\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The roots of the equation \\\\( x^2 - 4x + 4 = 0 \\\\) can be found by recognizing it as a perfect square: \\\\( (x - 2)^2 = 0 \\\\). Thus, the root is \\\\( x = 2 \\\\) (repeated).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}]'),(6,'2026-04-01','10','1.maths - circles, coordinate geometry, arithmetic progressions, pair of linear equations in two variables, polynomials\n2.science - sources of energy, electricity, light ,  reflection and refraction, heredity and evolution, how do organisms reproduce?, control and coordination, life processes, carbon and its compounds, metals and non-metals, chemical reactions and equations, chemical reactions','mock test',_binary '%PDF-1.3\n3 0 obj\n<</Type /Page\n/Parent 1 0 R\n/Resources 2 0 R\n/Contents 4 0 R>>\nendobj\n4 0 obj\n<</Filter /FlateDecode /Length 927>>\nstream\nxœ¥VMo\ã6½ï¯˜c‚\Ø\\‘¢(*@Ql²\İ~\ÖG£-162\éŠ\Ò:ş÷RòF¬\"@O¦†ofŞ¼!‡fğË»„d9\ß=¬\àı\'\n”“$\Õü°\n¦<%™€¼\È\ÍaUÁ\Íc­¼šÀ~W\í\Î/\à\Ï\İÉ›;½7¾mNx0®v[\\ü¨­nTı÷¯\Ök]mõ-¬¾±\ßb@\ÙEºh¢¦”Z@.8‘EdğQµúX\Â\Ä2I—)E°œF_\Ø\