\sin \\theta}{\\\\cos \\theta}\\\\). Since \\\\(\\tan \\theta = 3\\\\), \\\\(\\\\sin \\theta = 3 \\\\cos \\theta\\\\). The correct option is \\\\(\\frac{3}{\\\\sqrt{10}}\\\\) because \\\\(\\\\sin^2 \\theta + \\\\cos^2 \\theta = 1\\\\) and \\\\(\\\\sin \\theta = 3 \\\\cos \\theta\\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"In a right-angled triangle, if \\\\(\\\\sin \\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\\\), what is the value of \\\\(\\theta\\\\) in degrees?\", \"options\": [\"30 degrees\", \"45 degrees\", \"60 degrees\", \"90 degrees\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"The sine of 30 degrees is \\\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\\\). Therefore, \\\\(\\theta = 30\\\\) degrees.\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If \\\\(\\\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\), what is the value of \\\\(\\\\sin \\theta\\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"\\\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\\\)\", \"\\\\(\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\)\", \"\\\\(\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\\)\", \"\\\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\\\)\"], \"correct_answer\": \"B\", \"explanation\": \"Use the Pythagorean identity \\\\(\\\\sin^2 \\theta + \\\\cos^2 \\theta = 1\\\\). Given \\\\(\\\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\), \\\\(\\\\sin^2 \\theta = 1 - \\\\left(\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2 = 1 - \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{1}{4}\\\\). Therefore, \\\\(\\\\sin \\theta = \\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}, {\"question\": \"If \\\\(\\\\cot \\theta = 2\\\\), what is the value of \\\\(\\tan \\theta\\\\)?\", \"options\": [\"2\", \"1/2\", \"0.5\", \"0.25\"], \"correct_answer\": \"A\", \"explanation\": \"Cosecant and cotangent are reciprocals of sine and tangent respectively. If \\\\(\\\\cot \\theta = 2\\\\), then \\\\(\\tan \\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\\\).\", \"type\": \"mcq\"}]'),(8,'2026-04-07','10','1.maths - statistics, areas related to circles, circles, introduction to trigonometry, coordinate geometry, arithmetic progressions, quadratic equations, real numbers\n2.science - our environment, sources of energy, magnetic effects of electric current, elec